1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:05,464
Open the skin example from the lesson and set
the image type to Brightfield H and E.

2
00:00:05,704 --> 00:00:13,833
Zoom into the dark purple band near the edge,
the epidermis. We will use the same patch to
compare the Brush and Wand.

3
00:00:14,073 --> 00:00:22,212
The shapes in this video are practice regions.
We'll refine one of them and see its area
change in the QuPath measurement table.

4
00:00:23,402 --> 00:00:29,001
Select Brush. Position the cursor inside the
dark purple epidermis.

5
00:00:29,241 --> 00:00:37,050
Press and drag a short stroke, then release.
QuPath creates an annotation based on the path
of the brush.

6
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:44,389
Zoom in to work on finer edges. The area
covered by the brush changes with zoom at the
default settings.

7
00:00:45,568 --> 00:00:52,068
Switch to the Wand. Start with a clean copy of
the same image so you can compare the tools.

8
00:00:52,308 --> 00:01:00,632
Click at the starting point of the previous
Brush stroke. The Wand grows a region around
the click based on local image contrast.

9
00:01:00,872 --> 00:01:11,935
The Brush follows the stroke. The Wand includes
nearby pixels with a similar appearance.
Inspect the Wand result along the tissue edge
and wherever the stain fades.

10
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:21,369
Return to the Brush outline and select it. With
the Brush, you can start the stroke inside the
selected area to extend it.

11
00:01:21,609 --> 00:01:29,878
Drag from inside the outline toward the edge.
Hold Shift if you need to start adding from
just outside the selected annotation.

12
00:01:30,118 --> 00:01:38,182
Here the stroke crosses the tissue boundary.
Keep the added tissue, then remove the part
that extends onto the glass.

13
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:45,904
Keep the annotation selected. Hold Alt and
brush along the part that spills onto the
glass.

14
00:01:46,144 --> 00:01:53,723
Start the eraser stroke on the glass side and
follow the tissue edge. Release once the extra
area is gone.

15
00:01:53,963 --> 00:02:00,722
Check the corrected contour. Use small strokes
and zoom in further if you need a more precise
edge.

16
00:02:01,902 --> 00:02:09,606
Open Measure, then Show annotation
measurements. Find the row for the selected
annotation and the Area column.

17
00:02:09,846 --> 00:02:18,955
Here the three stages are saved as copies for
comparison. The area increases after extending
the stroke and drops after correcting the edge.

18
00:02:19,195 --> 00:02:28,724
The unit is square micrometers because this
slide is calibrated. Save the final annotation
to your project once you're satisfied with its
outline.
